course: dictionary
lesson: 8851
title: Reading clues about a strange bird
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out what a new word means from the words around it. «The shoebill is a huge bird with a beak like a shoe» tells you the shape of its bill, and bill is another word for beak. The clue is in the name too: shoe plus bill.
explain: Looks can fool us. «The shoebill looks like a stork» but scientists do not decide family by looks alone. They check genes and bodies, so the word stork in its common name is not the whole story.
explain: Read on for more clues. «It waits almost without moving before it lunges to grab fish» tells you it is patient, then quick. When a word is still unclear, check the context, then use a dictionary to confirm.
fact: A shoebill is a very large grey bird that lives in the swamps of East Africa.
fact: Its huge bill is shaped like a wooden shoe, and it uses it to catch fish, lungfish and even baby crocodiles.
fact: «Shoebill stork» is a common name, but the shoebill is not a true stork.
fact: Scientists now think its closest relatives are pelicans and hammerkops.
fact: Shoebills are threatened because swamps are drained and their eggs are taken.
exercise: «The shoebill waits almost without moving, then lunges to grab fish.» What does lunges mean? | Sings a soft song | *Moves suddenly and quickly forward to grab | Sleeps for a long time | Flies slowly away
exercise: What is the shoebill's bill shaped like? | *A wooden shoe | A stork's leg | A fish | A pelican's pouch
exercise: Where do shoebills live? | *The swamps of East Africa | The high mountains of Europe | The Australian desert | Northern Scotland
test: Why should you not judge a bird only by its looks? | *Because scientists check relatives by genes and bodies | Because shoebills have no bills | Because looks always tell the truth | Because all birds look the same
test: What do shoebills greet each other by doing? | Flying in circles | Singing high notes | *Clattering their huge beaks | Swimming under the water
exam: What does the word stork tell you about the shoebill, and why can it be misleading? | *It is a common name, but scientists think the shoebill is not a true stork | It shows the shoebill is closely related to the crocodile | It means the shoebill is a type of fish | It means the shoebill can fly faster than any other bird
